Sorry, I didn't give a complete explanation.  The first set of results that got PRESENCE and occu with essentially the same estimates was after dividing VegHt by 10.  Hence, the estimates of the VegHt coefficient and standard error were 10 times the size of the analysis with the untransformed VegHt.

The output from the analysis with Mathematica used the original units of VegHt (i.e., no division) to match with Bob's original analysis.

